{"availability":"available","full":"HandoT/wastimate","name":"wastimate","description":"Python package for calculating the flow of radioactive materials","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2024-05-02T11:57:30Z","updated":"2026-10-02T12:21:39Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://handot.github.io/wastimate/","topics":[],"demo":"https://handot.github.io/wastimate/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.213Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.213Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.213Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.213Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["wastimate is a Python package for simulating the time evolution of radioactive waste inventories, accounting for radioactive decay and the transfer of material between locations. Given a description of a set of waste packages, their locations, and the rules governing their movement or introduction over time, the package computes mass, volume, activity, and heat output at arbitrary points in the simulated timeline.","The package is intended for inventory and dose-relevant quantity estimation in waste management contexts: projecting activity or heat output at a future date, evaluating the effect of decay on short-lived isotopes within a package, or tracking total inventory at a facility as material is added, removed, or transferred according to a defined schedule."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HandoT/wastimate/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2a7edbe9b1b0ece9307ace12ec370c20d98f4f8e5f07cddfa9360dc5d0c5c40c","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.432Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.432Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"wastimate is a Python package for simulating the time evolution of radioactive waste inventories, accounting for radioactive decay and the transfer of material between locations. Given a description of a set of waste packages, their locations, and the rules governing their movement or introduction over time, the package computes mass, volume, activity, and heat output at arbitrary points in the simulated timeline.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HandoT/wastimate/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"The package is intended for inventory and dose-relevant quantity estimation in waste management contexts: projecting activity or heat output at a future date, evaluating the effect of decay on short-lived isotopes within a package, or tracking total inventory at a facility as material is added, removed, or transferred according to a defined schedule.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HandoT/wastimate/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"2a7edbe9b1b0ece9307ace12ec370c20d98f4f8e5f07cddfa9360dc5d0c5c40c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HandoT/wastimate/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.432Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-02T12:21:39Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/HandoT/wastimate/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:52.433Z","hash":"2a7edbe9b1b0ece9307ace12ec370c20d98f4f8e5f07cddfa9360dc5d0c5c40c","originalBytes":5148,"storedBytes":5148,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["model","output","package","packages","time","parameter","specified","any","carlo","executed","monte","defined","distribution","node","simulation","activity","decay","execution","heat","interface","inventory","may","nuclide","values","waste","aggregated","application","defines","each","file","function","including","mass","material","nodes","radioactive","rather","results","simulated","single","tabular","their","transfer","trial","trials","wastimate","xml","according","across","alongside","automatically","computed","configuration","data","data.","during","ensemble","every","execution.","fixed","given","import","imported","individual","inspection","introduction","inventories","json","mult